[ledge] Required blind insert-pocket ends. Each Ø4 mm bottom pilot retains its specified cylindrical depth plus the 0.25 mm supported-face allowance; the flat end bridges the 4 mm opening in the upright shell. Its position preserves insert room and the M3x25 screw-tip allowance recorded in the casing integration receipt.
alternatives: A taper at the same end plane shortens the full-depth cylindrical seat. Extending that taper deeper changes the specified pocket-end datum. A through-bore opens the pocket beyond its blind end. The current slice retains localized bridge cooling and no supports in these small blind pockets.
