[sliver] The linter is wrong here: these strips are the 1.0 mm side walls of the seam channel and of its fold, faces of a recess with the full 2.38 mm section behind them, not a ligament thinner than 1.6 mm. Their depth is the channel's depth, and the channel walls are the inside corners the outer wall's seam is placed in.
alternatives: Walls deeper than 1.6 mm bring the fold within 0.6 mm of the PRV shroud's cap end. Sloped walls leave the axis-aligned check but open the inside corners the seam is placed in.
